    <string name="policy_title">Privacy &amp; terms</string>
    <string name="policy_subtitle">Please read this before using Vectr. Required for Google Play compliance.</string>
    <string name="policy_accept_label">I have read and accept the privacy policy</string>
    <string name="policy_must_accept">Accept the privacy policy to continue</string>
    <string name="policy_full_text">Privacy Policy — Vectr (DMTech)\n\nLast updated: July 21, 2026\n\n1. Who we are\nVectr is a local mobile IDE with an optional AI agent, developed by DMTech. The app runs on your device.\n\n2. Data we process\n• API keys and preferences are stored on your device (encrypted prefs where applicable).\n• Project files you open via the system file picker stay under your control (SAF). Vectr does not upload your project to our servers.\n• Chat history is stored locally in an on-device database.\n• When you use the agent, prompts and tool results are sent to the AI provider YOU configure (e.g. DeepSeek or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint). We do not operate that API.\n\n3. Optional network features\n• Web search / fetch_url may contact third-party sites (e.g. DuckDuckGo) to answer questions.\n• Notifications (Android 13+) show when the agent works in the background — only if you allow them.\n\n4. Optional Termux integration\n• Vectr can ask Termux to run shell commands you confirm in the chat.\n• This requires Termux and Termux:Tasker installed from F-Droid, plus the special permission “Run commands in Termux environment”.\n• Commands are never executed silently without your confirmation in the app UI.\n• Termux is optional. You can skip it and still use files, editor, and the agent (without shell tools).\n\n5. Permissions summary\n• Notifications — progress of background AI work.\n• Termux RUN_COMMAND — only to run confirmed shell commands via Termux.\n• Storage access — only folders/files you explicitly open.\n\n6. Children\nVectr is not directed at children under 13.\n\n7. Contact\nDeveloper: DMTech. App: Vectr.\n\n8. Changes\nWe may update this policy in app updates. Continued use after an update means you accept the revised text shown at first launch / in Settings.</string>

    <string name="perm_title">Permissions</string>
    <string name="perm_subtitle">Grant only what you need. Termux is optional and explained below.</string>
    <string name="perm_notif_title">Notifications</string>
    <string name="perm_notif_desc">Shows when the agent is working in the background so Android does not silently kill the stream.</string>
    <string name="perm_termux_title">Run commands in Termux</string>
    <string name="perm_termux_desc">Special permission so Vectr can ask Termux to run a command you confirm. Without it, shell tools stay disabled.</string>
    <string name="perm_install_title">Install Termux (F-Droid)</string>
    <string name="perm_install_steps">1. Install F-Droid (if needed).\n2. Install Termux (com.termux).\n3. Install Termux:Tasker (com.termux.tasker).\n4. Open Termux once, then return here and allow the permission.\n\nPlay Store builds of Termux are outdated — use F-Droid.</string>
